    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "285ff23470e75fe31add8b78746c7441",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"massive-quarkgluon-scattering\">Massive quark\u2013gluon scattering</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/qcd_gluons.py\">Quark annihilation to gluons</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/gluon_scattering.py\">Gluon scattering</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate the three <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(qg\\to qg||)</marimo-tex> diagrams and every interference term, retaining\nthe quark mass and symbolic SU(<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(N_c||)</marimo-tex>) color algebra. The model's bottom quark\nsupplies the generic mass; particles and vertices are selected by name.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Compare two independent routes from the FeynCalc examples:\n<a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QCD/Tree/QGl-QGl\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">physical gluon polarizations</a>\nand <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QCD/Tree/QGl-QGl-2\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">covariant sums with ghost subtraction</a>.\nShared particle spin/color sums, Spenso and Idenso perform the contractions.\nBoth null and timelike gauge references give the same massive result.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The initial symbolic calculation runs once. The controls reuse its results.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "2255469496942f7eefdc8810f478bd99",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": [
        {
          "type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": "color ghG\nspin ghG\nLorentz structures ghG 1\nFinished ghG ghost\ncolor ghG~\nspin ghG~\nLorentz structures ghG~ 1\nFinished ghG~ ghost\ncolor g\nspin g\nLorentz structures g 107\nFinished g covariant\nFinished g null\nFinished g timelike\nMassive SU(N) quark-gluon scattering, physical gauges, ghost subtraction and massless reference passed\n",
          "mimetype": "text/plain"
        }
